{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Implementation evidence (commit 4f8cd749a61, not yet pushed)\n\n**Compelling-reason check for an exact pin (operator Step 1): none found.**\n- (a) Lock churn: on a scratch copy without required-version, uv 0.12.7 and uv 0.13.6 both pass `uv lock --check` and rewrite uv.lock (version 1, revision 5) byte-identically. `validate-locks` covers the review-scanner locks, not uv.lock.\n- (b) Supply chain: the checksum-verified install needs one concrete version to download, not an exact `required-version`; the version now lives in the action's `UV_VERSION` beside its checksums.\n- (c) Incidents: 56b7-b21a-c8ab-4afc and 5caa-4b63-7ea2-4e71 were CI manifest fetches, fixed by CI knowing a concrete version (kept). 2d87-7428-abcf-4bd9 and corking-phonolite-drafthorse were failures caused BY the exact pin.\n- (d) Docs: no ADR or doc requires an exact uv pin; releasing.md lists SBOM tooling as post-1.0.\n- Floor capability (live run, uv 0.13.6): `>=0.12.7` passes; `>=0.13.7` is refused with \"Required uv version `>=0.13.7` does not match the running version `0.13.6`\".\n\n**RED** (new tests against the old implementation): `pytest tests/unit/test_uv_pin_guard.py` -> 22 failed, 28 passed (including all 5 non-floor specifier cases, the 3 UV_VERSION cases, and the above-floor Dockerfile case); `tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py` failed at collection because pyproject still held `==`.\n**GREEN**: both files -> 59 passed. `python scripts/check_uv_pin.py` rc=0; `uv lock --check` rc=0 under uv 0.13.6; `make lint` rc=0; `make typecheck` rc=0; `check_mechanism_delta.py --check` rc=0. `git grep -nF '==0.13.6' -- docs pyproject.toml Makefile` -> no hits; `>=0.12.7` appears 2 times in docs/local-dev-env.md."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793762005012912001,"uuid":"19f48214-0251-49dc-a3e2-01c8d9be3824"}